## MLM Web App in Node.js

**Product:** "HealthyGlow" - a skincare product line

**Web App:**

```js
const express = require('express');
const app = express();

app.get('/products', (req, res) => {
  res.send({
    products: [
      { name: 'HealthyGlow Cleanser', description: 'Gentle cleanser for all skin types', price: 20 },
      { name: 'HealthyGlow Serum', description: 'Hydrating serum with natural ingredients', price: 30 },
      { name: 'HealthyGlow Moisturizer', description: 'Nourishing moisturizer for soft, supple skin', price: 25 }
    ]
  });
});

app.post('/order', (req, res) => {
  const order = req.body;
  console.log("Order:", order);
  res.send({ message: "Order received!" });
});

app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log("Server listening on port 3000");
});
```

**Python Script:**

```python
import requests

# Replace with your MLM website URL
url = "localhost:3000"

# Define your custom order
order = {
  name: "John Doe",
  address: "123 Main St.",
  products: [
    {"name": "HealthyGlow Cleanser", "quantity": 2},
    {"name": "HealthyGlow Serum", "quantity": 1},
    {"name": "HealthyGlow Moisturizer", "quantity": 3}
  ]
}

# Send order request
response = requests.post(url + "/order", json=order)

# Check if order was successful
if response.status_code == 200:
  print("Order successful!")
else:
  print("Error:", response.text)
```

**Additional Notes:**

* This script assumes you have already created a user account on the MLM website.
* You will need to modify the `url` variable to point to your actual MLM website.
* You can also customize the `order` dictionary to include any additional information you want to include with your order.
* You can add more products to the `products` list in the

